egl/wayland: honour LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2 to run Zink without a render node

On X11, MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=zink with LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2=1 skips the
render node checks and presents through kopper (Vulkan WSI). Wayland had no
equivalent: without wl_drm or dma-buf feedback from the compositor there is
no fd_render_gpu, the DRM init fails and eglInitialize falls back to
llvmpipe. Setting LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1 does reach the kopper path, but
Zink then insists on a CPU Vulkan device. On Termux the GPU is reachable only
through Turnip on KGSL, and there is no /dev/dri at all.

With Zink requested (on Termux that is also the default, see 0017) and
LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2 set, take the wl_shm/kopper init without LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE,
so Zink picks the hardware Vulkan device. Forced Zink has no DRM node for an
EGLDevice, and the software EGLDevice would mark it unaccelerated, so the
display gets none. Without LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2, with LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE, and on
X11 nothing changes. If Zink cannot start, eglInitialize still falls back to
llvmpipe.

Applies on top of 0012-always-use-software-for-swrast.patch.
Informed by Local Desktop's egl-wayland-zink-kopper-without-render-node patch
(same idea; this one is written against Mesa 26.3.1 and Termux's patch set,
and leaves X11 and surfaceless untouched).

--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c	2026-11-24 01:04:58.017514199 +0300
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c	2026-11-24 01:05:25.546070975 +0300
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 
 #include "util/anon_file.h"
 #include "util/perf/cpu_trace.h"
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
 #include "util/u_vector.h"
 #include "util/format/u_formats.h"
 #include "main/glconfig.h"
@@ -3252,6 +3253,17 @@
    .swrast = &swrast_loader_extension,
 };
 
+/* LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2 means what it means on X11: run Zink on the Vulkan device
+ * and present through kopper (Vulkan WSI) without a DRM render node, for
+ * compositors that offer neither wl_drm nor dma-buf feedback.
+ */
+static bool
+dri2_wl_force_zink(const _EGLDisplay *disp)
+{
+   return disp->Options.Zink && !disp->Options.ForceSoftware &&
+          debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2", false);
+}
+
 static EGLBoolean
 dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 {
@@ -3303,10 +3315,14 @@
    if (!dri2_create_screen(disp))
       goto cleanup;
 
+   /* Forced Zink has no DRM node to describe, and the software EGLDevice
+    * would mark it unaccelerated, so it gets no EGLDevice.
+    */
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
-   if (!dri2_setup_device(disp, true)) {
+   if (!dri2_wl_force_zink(disp) && !dri2_setup_device(disp, true)) {
 #else
-   if (!dri2_setup_device(disp, disp->Options.ForceSoftware)) {
+   if (!dri2_wl_force_zink(disp) &&
+       !dri2_setup_device(disp, disp->Options.ForceSoftware)) {
 #endif
       _eglError(EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED, "DRI2: failed to setup EGLDevice");
       goto cleanup;
@@ -3342,7 +3358,7 @@
 EGLBoolean
 dri2_initialize_wayland(_EGLDisplay *disp)
 {
-   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware)
+   if (disp->Options.ForceSoftware || dri2_wl_force_zink(disp))
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_swrast(disp);
    else
       return dri2_initialize_wayland_drm(disp);
